TER-AI data licenses
====================

The code of terai-router is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). One bundled data file is not:

src/terai_router/data/knowledge_th.json  (TER-AI Thai knowledge pack, v0.8.0)

  Source:    Thai Wikipedia (https://th.wikipedia.org), lead sections of articles,
             retrieved 2026-10-16.
  Authors:   Wikipedia contributors. The authors of each article are listed in its
             page history: https://th.wikipedia.org/?curid=<id> (the id of every entry
             is stored in the file).
  License:   Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  Changes:   Wiki markup, tables, references and templates removed; text converted to
             plain text and shortened to the lead section; a search index added.
             Built by training/build_knowledge.py.

  This file, as an adaptation of Wikipedia text, is distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
  If you share it or a modified version, keep this attribution and the same license.
  Every answer the Chat class gives from this file ends with the article title and
  "CC BY-SA 4.0" so the source stays visible to the person reading it.

src/terai_router/muml_wa/data/markov.json  (MuML 1.0 WA note table, Markov v1, since v0.12.0)
docs/muml_wa_table.js                      (the same table for the web demo's MuML tab)

  Source:    Nottingham Music Database (original ABC files: http://abc.sourceforge.net/NMD/),
             as cleaned by jukedeck/nottingham-dataset
             (https://github.com/jukedeck/nottingham-dataset, commit
             0992bb6cd864f6d4b90d6663e08c0ef53ffaa08f), tokenized for MuML 1.0.
  License:   GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0-only), the license of that dataset
             (its LICENSE.md is the GPL-3.0 text). The full text ships next to each data file:
             src/terai_router/muml_wa/data/LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt and docs/LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt.
  Contents:  counts only: which key-relative pitch follows which, which chord follows which,
             and which whole-bar rhythms occur. No tune is stored. Built by
             training/muml_wa/build_table.py (that script is code, MIT).
  Marking:   markov.json has a "license" entry and docs/muml_wa_table.js has a license
             header; both name the source. docs/muml_wa_table.js is a byte copy of
             markov.json (checked by eval/parity.py and tests/test_muml_wa_js_parity.py).

  These two data files are distributed under GPL-3.0. If you share them or a modified
  version, keep this attribution and the GPL-3.0 license. They are kept as separate files,
  so the code that reads them (src/terai_router/muml_wa/__init__.py, docs/muml_wa.js,
  docs/index.html and the rest of the repository) stays MIT.

All other files in src/terai_router/data/ (model.json, typo_pairs.json,
